>
  <p slot="lede">
    Niche games tend to have fragmented communities and scattered events: join a new Discord server for every tournament, and hope you catch event announcements in time. I built Midweek Mashers as a hub for MBAACC and FPAN online events. It's the original hub for Adomi-san and built to onboard other organizers in the scene to run their own events to centralize more events in one place.
  </p>
  <p class="contact__lede" slot="outro">
    Playing Melty Blood, developing a community, or want to talk about running events? <a href="https://x.com/enpicie" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em class="serif-italic">Find me on X</em></a>.
  </p>
</FeaturesPage>
